sd: no space between Asian and Latin text from PowerPoint

Edit engine puts a quarter-em gap between Asian and Latin text by
default; Impress turns it off only for Korean and Japanese. PowerPoint
never adds the gap, and DrawingML has no attribute for it, so a
PowerPoint title like "北京市2025年" drew wider in Impress, with a gap
around "2025" (Ely #83). PPTX and PPT import now turn the default off,
for the slides read and the text added later.
